    "body": "### Problem\n\nClosing a window from inside a TermClose autocmd removes the window but fires no WinClosed. Deferring the same call out of the handler with `vim.schedule` fires it.\n\n`:help WinClosed` says it fires \"When closing a window, just before it is removed from the window layout\", and notes only that the event cannot trigger itself, so I can't tell from the docs whether this is deliberate re-entrancy protection or a gap.\n\nIt matters downstream because a plugin that closes its own floating terminal from TermClose (snacks.nvim does this for lazygit) leaves other plugins with no window-close event to react to.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`nvim --clean`, then `:luafile` this:\n\n```lua\nlocal win = vim.api.nvim_open_win(vim.api.nvim_create_buf(false, true), true, {\n  relative = \"editor\", row = 1, col = 1, width = 40, height = 10,\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"WinClosed\", {\n  callback = function(ev)\n    print(\"WinClosed fired for window \" .. ev.match)\n  end,\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"TermClose\", {\n  callback = function()\n    vim.api.nvim_win_close(win, true)\n    print(\"closed from TermClose, win valid: \" .. tostring(vim.api.nvim_win_is_valid(win)))\n  end,\n})\n\nvim.fn.jobstart({ \"sh\", \"-c\", \"sleep 0.3\" }, { term = true })\n```\n\nThen `:messages`.\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nWinClosed fires when the window is removed.\n\n### Actual behaviour\n\n```\nclosed from TermClose, win valid: false\n```\n\nNo WinClosed line. Wrapping the `nvim_win_close` call in `vim.schedule` gives both:\n\n```\nWinClosed fired for window 1001\nclosed via vim.schedule, win valid: false\n```\n\n### Version\n\nNVIM v0.12.5, Build type: Release, LuaJIT 2.1.1774638290, on Ubuntu under WSL2.",
